UPDATE companies SET description='Fisher Textiles, based in Matthews, North Carolina, has supplied engineered fabrics for digital textile printing since 1988. Founded as a textile converting operation, the company pivoted in the mid-1990s to develop polyester fabrics specifically for wide-format dye sublimation, establishing itself in the emerging soft signage market. In 2023, a strategic investment from American Pacific Group (APG) brought new capital and made Fisher Textiles a sister company to digital print production partner Media One.

The company produces knit and woven fabrics compatible with dye sublimation, direct dye sublimation, UV, latex, pigment, and solvent ink systems, with widths up to 197 inches. Its 82,000-square-foot headquarters, opened in 2019, houses expanded warehousing, a print demonstration room, and training space. Nine distribution centers across the U.S. and Canada — including locations in California, Nevada, Texas, Florida, Wisconsin, South Carolina, and Ontario — stock popular products for faster delivery.

Fisher Textiles serves the trade show exhibit, SEG display, retail graphics, backlit signage, banner, home furnishings, gaming table, and performance apparel markets. Its recycled-fabric line uses post-consumer PET bottles, and a take-back program repurposes used signage into new fiber-based products.

The company emphasizes quality consistency, technical expertise, fast response, reliable inventory, and long-term customer partnerships — values maintained from its early days in a 3,000-square-foot leased facility to its current national footprint.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Textile converting", "Dye sublimation fabric engineering", "Direct dye sublimation fabric engineering", "UV printable fabric engineering", "Latex printable fabric engineering", "Pigment printable fabric engineering", "Solvent ink compatible fabric engineering", "Fabric recycling program", "Custom roll slitting", "Sample fulfillment"], "industries": ["Digital textile printing", "Graphics and signage", "Trade show exhibits", "SEG displays", "Retail graphics", "Backlit signage", "Banner production", "Home furnishings", "Gaming tables", "Performance apparel"], "materials": ["Polyester", "Cotton", "Recycled polyester (post-consumer PET)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nine distribution centers in the U.S. and Canada reducing shipping costs and delivery times", "82,000 sq ft headquarters with print demonstration room and training facilities", "Fabric recycling program using post-consumer PET bottles and take-back of used signage", "Award-winning fabrics recognized by PRINTING United Alliance (2026)", "Engineered fabrics supporting six print technologies including dye sublimation, UV, latex, and solvent"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 -> db", "Headquarters Matthews, NC -> db", "82,000 sq ft HQ opened 2019 -> /about-us", "Nine distribution centers listed -> /", "Strategic investment from APG 2023 -> /about-us", "Sister company Media One -> /about-us", "Fabrics for dye sub, UV, latex, solvent -> /", "Widths up to 197 inches -> /", "Applications: trade shows, retail lightboxes, SEG, backlit, banners, home furnishings, gaming tables, performance apparel -> /about-us", "Recycled fabrics from post-consumer PET bottles -> /