UPDATE companies SET description='Franklin Braid Manufacturing operates from Emporia, Virginia, where it has been based since 1956. The business traces its roots to 1944, when Wick Narrow Fabric Company purchased a plant in Franklin, Virginia, to produce flat braided tapes. In 1980 the company became a subsidiary of Wayne Mills, a family-owned textile mill founded in 1910 in Philadelphia, and the two remain sister operations today.

Its 80,000-square-foot facility employs 90 people and runs at a rate exceeding 20 million feet of product per week.

Franklin Braid serves a global customer base across apparel, bags, home furnishings, medical, outdoor, agriculture, fishing, military, filtration, awning, and other industrial markets. Customers range from military-grade specifiers to consumer-goods brands seeking bulk volumes of polyester, cotton, nylon, and other yarn-based products.

