UPDATE companies SET description='Freedom Truck & Trailer Parts was founded in October 2002 in Salt Lake City, Utah. The company began as a Utah Subchapter S corporation and later reorganized as a limited liability company. It remains locally owned and managed, operating from a 28,000-square-foot warehouse and manufacturing facility in the city''s transportation and industrial hub.

The company distributes a broad line of heavy-duty truck and trailer components — including air brakes, driveline parts, engine rebuild kits, suspension, lighting, and filtration — sourced from brands such as Meritor, Dana/Spicer, Eaton, Grote, and Baldwin. In addition to distribution, Freedom runs an in-house gear remanufacturing shop that rebuilds heavy-duty transmissions and differentials using only genuine OEM parts, and a brake shoe relining facility that applies premium friction materials. The facility stocks hundreds of remanufactured units for quick turnaround, and the company also provides private-label manufacturing for dealers and warehouse distributors.

The company also supplies private-label remanufactured units to other dealers and warehouse distributors.

The company emphasizes a ''home-grown'' service philosophy, aiming to minimize downtime by keeping remanufactured units in stock and eliminating middleman costs through in-house production. It highlights its use of genuine OEM components in all rebuilds, comprehensive warranties, and a commitment to fair, competitive pricing backed by its membership in the VIPER Heavy Duty purchasing group.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Heavy-duty transmission remanufacturing", "Differential remanufacturing", "Brake shoe relining", "Heavy truck and trailer parts distribution", "Online parts ordering", "Nationwide shipping", "Private label manufacturing", "OEM parts sourcing", "Technical consultation and troubleshooting"], "industries": ["Heavy truck", "Trailer", "Commercial vehicle", "Transportation", "Fleet maintenance", "Aftermarket parts distribution"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["28,000 sq ft warehouse and manufacturing facility in Salt Lake City", "In-house gear remanufacturing shop using only genuine OEM parts", "State-of-the-art brake shoe relining facility with premium friction materials", "Hundreds of remanufactured transmissions and differentials stocked for quick turnaround", "Private-label manufacturing for dealers and warehouse distributors", "Member of VIPER Heavy Duty national purchasing group"], "facts_used": ["Founded October 2002 as Utah Sub S Corporation -> /about-us", "Headquarters at 1153 S. 3600 W., Salt Lake City, Utah -> /about-us", "Locally owned and managed, Utah LLC -> /about-us", "28,000 sq ft warehouse and manufacturing facility -> /about-us", "In-house gear remanufacturing shop for transmissions and differentials -> /about-us", "Brake shoe relining facility with premium friction materials -> /about-us", "Hundreds of remanufactured units stocked for quick turnaround -> /about-us", "Private label manufacturing for dealers and W.D. -> /", "Member of VIPER H