UPDATE companies SET description='Fujirebio Diagnostics, Inc. is headquartered in Malvern, Pennsylvania, and operates as a wholly owned subsidiary of Japan’s H.U. Group Holdings Inc. The company’s founding year and original founders are not disclosed in public materials.

The company develops and manufactures in vitro diagnostic (IVD) products, including the fully automated Lumipulse® platform, assay kits for neurodegenerative and other conditions, instruments, software, controls, and raw materials. It also operates as a contract development and manufacturing organization (CDMO), offering partners end-to-end services from biomarker research through clinical validation, regulatory submission, and commercial production. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not published.

Its product portfolio spans neurology (Alzheimer’s, multiple sclerosis, Parkinson’s, ALS), oncology, infectious disease, autoimmune disorders, cardiac markers, diabetes, fertility, and transplantation. Recent collaborations include a letter of intent with Alzinova for a blood-based Alzheimer’s test and a sales partnership with Sysmex for dementia testing. Regulatory clearances include FDA-cleared biomarkers for blood-based Alzheimer’s diagnosis, CE marking for pTau 217 and NfL assays, Health Canada Class II licenses, and ANVISA authorization in Brazil.

Fujirebio emphasizes an open partnership model, providing diagnostic raw materials, reagents, and full development-to-manufacturing services to other technology providers. The company states that revenues from these partnerships are reinvested into R&D to fuel its innovation engine, aiming to multiply breakthroughs across diagnostic platforms and reach more patients than it could alone.', certifications=ARRAY['CE MARKING','FDA-CLEARED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["IVD biomarker research and innovation", "Contract development and manufacturing (CDMO)", "Diagnostic raw material and reagent supply", "Full development, manufacturing, clinical and regulatory services", "Fully automated immunoassay testing (Lumipulse platform)", "Manual and semi-automated assay kits", "Diagnostic software development", "Control and calibrator production", "Clinical validation and regulatory submission support"], "industries": ["In vitro diagnostics", "Neurology", "Oncology", "Infectious diseases", "Autoimmune diseases", "Cardiac diagnostics", "Diabetes", "Fertility", "Genetic disorders", "Transplantation", "Bone metabolism", "Hypertension", "Inflammation", "Interstitial pneumonia"], "materials": ["Diagnostic raw materials", "Reagents", "Controls", "Calibrators"], "equipment": ["Lumipulse\u00ae platform", "Lumipulse G NfL Blood assay", "Lumipulse G pTau 217 Plasma assay", "Lumipulse G pTau 217 CSF assay"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Open partnership model covering raw materials through full regulatory and manufacturing services", "FDA-cleared blood-based biomarkers for Alzheimer\u2019s disease", "Proprietary Lumipulse\u00ae platform for clinical validation", "Reinvestment of CDMO partnership revenues into internal R&D", "Multi-region regulatory approvals (FDA, CE, Health Canada, ANVISA)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Malvern, Pennsylvania -> db", "Wholly owned subsidiary of H.U. Group Holdings Inc. -> /", "IVD biomarker innovation and CDMO s