UPDATE companies SET description='Born and raised in Oregon, they recognized a need for a legitimate, reputable solar company that could serve both Oregon and Washington with integrity. From the start, the founders have remained hands‑on, working alongside their installation crews in the field.

The company designs and installs solar photovoltaic systems, battery storage, and EV chargers for residential, commercial, and municipal customers. Its services include custom system design, free consultation, professional installation, mobile monitoring setup, and ongoing maintenance such as panel cleaning, repair, and removal/reinstallation for roof work. Green Ridge Solar partners with SolarEdge for inverters and monitoring and with FranklinWH for battery storage, and backs every installation with a 25‑year workmanship warranty.

Customers range from homeowners seeking lower bills and backup power to farms, nonprofits, and government agencies. Notable projects include a 31.68 kW rooftop system for the Marion County Evidence Building in Salem, a ground‑mount array with four batteries for a Bend family, a horse‑farm installation in Brush Prairie, Washington, and a third‑party‑ownership solar install in Madras, Oregon. The company also services systems originally installed by other providers.

Green Ridge Solar differentiates itself through a zero‑pressure consultation model, deep local knowledge of Pacific Northwest permitting and incentives, and a dedicated service contact—known as ''Sam, the Service Savior''—who coordinates rapid response to any system issue. The founders started the business to provide a trustworthy, community‑focused alternative in a market they felt lacked integrity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design", "Solar panel installation", "Battery storage installation (FranklinWH)", "EV charger installation", "Solar system maintenance and repair", "Solar panel cleaning", "Solar panel removal and reinstallation for roof work", "Solar system upgrades and retrofits", "Third-party ownership (TPO) solar installation", "Commercial solar installation", "Municipal/government solar projects", "Agricultural solar installation", "Custom solar design", "Free solar consultation", "Mobile monitoring setup", "Roof-mounted solar installation", "Ground-mounted solar installation", "Solar inverter installation (SolarEdge)", "Production monitoring", "Solar service for third-party installed systems"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Municipal/Government", "Agricultural", "Nonprofit", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["SolarEdge inverters", "FranklinWH batteries"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-pressure consultation model", "25-year workmanship warranty on all installations", "Dedicated service contact (Sam) for rapid issue resolution", "Local expertise in PNW climate, permitting, and incentives", "Partnerships with SolarEdge inverters and FranklinWH batteries"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2016 by Alex and Brian in Sherwood, Oregon -> db", "Serves Oregon and Washington -> db, /", "Provides solar installation, battery backup, EV charging, maintenance, cleaning, panel removal/reinstall -> /, /services", "Uses SolarEdge inverters and FranklinWH batteries -> /", "Offers 25-year workmanship warranty -> /", "Zero-pressure consultation -> /", "Dedicated service contact Sam -> /", "Completed projects for Marion County Evidence Building (31.68 kW), residential in Bend, Boring, etc. -> /services", "Serves residential, commercial, municipal, agricultural, nonprofit sectors -> /, /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Green Ridge Solar delivered the complete 31.68 kW rooftop solar system", "founded_year": "2016", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='green-ridge-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Griffin Foods is headquartered in Muskogee, Oklahoma, where it was founded in 1908 by brothers John T. and Charles M. Griffin. The company began as the Griffin Grocery Company in McAlester before moving to Muskogee in 1923, when John Griffin built a three-story facility housing administration, warehousing, and processing. Now a fourth-generation, family-owned and minority-owned business, it operates under the Griffin Holding Company alongside Griffin Communications.

The company specializes in manufacturing and packaging liquid and emulsified semi-solid food products, with core lines in table syrups, mustards, molasses, imitation vanilla, and corn syrups. Through its 2006 acquisition of House of Webster in Rogers, Arkansas, Griffin added gourmet jams, jellies, preserves, fruit butters, relishes, salsas, barbecue sauces, salad dressings, and pickled products. It offers co-packing and private-label services, formulating new products or running customer formulas, and packages in retail, foodservice, and industrial sizes. The Muskogee facility serves distribution across the continental U.S., Mexico, and Europe; by 2000 the company employed roughly 100 people and recorded several million dollars in annual sales.

Griffin supplies food manufacturers, foodservice distributors, and retail grocery chains, with its branded products stocked in most Oklahoma-area supermarkets. Major customers receive branded, private-label, and co-packed items, and the company sells direct by the case.

Griffin differentiates itself through food-safety certifications—SQF Food Safety Code for Food Manufacturing and Kosher Parve certification from the Orthodox Union—and a commitment to allergen-free production (no Big 8 allergens). The company emphasizes quick response, high-grade ingredients, and a track record of customer-service awards.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Food Safety Code for Food Manufacturing','Kosher Parve (Orthodox Union)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Liquid food product manufacturing", "Emulsified semi-solid food product manufacturing", "Packaging (retail, foodservice, industrial)", "Co-packing", "Private label manufacturing", "Product formulation (NBE)", "Table syrup production", "Mustard production", "Molasses production", "Imitation vanilla production", "Corn syrup production", "Gourmet jam, jelly, preserve production", "Fruit spread production", "Fruit butter production", "Relish production", "Salsa production", "Barbecue sauce production", "Salad dressing production", "Pickled product production"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Foodservice", "Retail grocery", "Private label", "Co-packing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SQF Food Safety Code certified", "Kosher Parve certified by Orthodox Union", "Minority-owned, family-operated fourth generation", "Co-packing and private label with formulation capabilities", "No Big 8 allergens packed"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1908 by John T. and Charles M. Griffin -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Muskogee, Oklahoma -> /about-us", "Family-owned, minority-owned, fourth generation -> /about-us", "Specializes in liquid and emulsified semi-solid food products: table syrups, mustards, molasses, imitation vanilla, corn syrups -> /", "Offers co-packing and private label with formulation capabilities -> /about-us", "Acquired House of Webster in 2006 adding gourmet jams, jellies, preserves, etc. -> /about-us", "Certified to SQF Food Safety Code for Food Manufacturing -> /about-us", "Certified Kosher Parve by Orthodox Union -> /about-us", "No Big 8 allergens packed -> /about-us", "Distribution across continental US, Mexico, Europe -> /about-us", "Employed approximately 100 individuals by 2000 -> /about-us", "Sells by the case directly to customers -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Griffin Food Company specializes in the production and packaging of liquid and emulsified semi-solid based food products.", "founded_year": "1908", "employee_count": "approximately 100 (as of 2000)", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 case", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='griffin-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Grote Company is a family-owned manufacturer of industrial food slicing and assembly equipment based in Columbus, Ohio. Founded in 1972 by Jim Grote, the company began as a specialist in food processing machinery and has remained under family ownership for over five decades.

The company designs and builds three primary equipment lines: pizza topping lines that automate sauce depositing, pepperoni slicing, and cheese or IQF ingredient application; sandwich assembly lines that combine fixed equipment and robotics for depositing, slicing, assembling, aligning, and cutting; and a range of food slicers from multi-purpose offline models to high-speed multi-lane industrial units. Beyond hardware, Grote provides parts and blade ordering, training, equipment health assessments, field service, reconditioning, and replacement support, and operates demo facilities for customer product testing.

Grote serves food processors worldwide, including frozen pizza manufacturers, sandwich producers, meat processors slicing pepperoni and other proteins, jerky makers such as Las Vegas Jerky''s, and bakery operations. Reference customers cited include Kunzler & Company and Martel Foods, which automated sandwich lidding with Grote robotics.

